  "question": {
    "text": "Among $10^{-9} \\mathrm{~g}$ (each) of the following elements, which one will have the highest number of atoms? Element : $\\mathrm{Pb}, \\mathrm{Po}, \\mathrm{Pr}$ and Pt",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "A9LkC",
      "text": "Po",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MJaAp",
      "text": "Pr",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "nqD4U",
      "text": "Pb",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1iA4j",
      "text": "Pt",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\text { No. of atoms }=\\frac{\\text { Massin } g}{\\operatorname{Molar} \\operatorname{Mas}(\\mathrm{~g} / \\mathrm{mol})} \\times \\mathrm{N}_{\\mathrm{A}}$<br />Therefore for the same Mass element having the least Molar mass will have the higher no. of atoms.<br />- $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{Po}}=209$<br />- $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{Pr}}=141$<br />- $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{Pb}}=207$<br />- $\\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{Pt}}=195$",
    "image": null
  },
